  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The difference in energy between the actual structure and the lowest energy resonance structure for the given compound is known as resonance energy.</p><p>The resonance energy of a compound is a measure of the extra stability of the conjugated system compared to the corresponding number of isolated double bonds.</p>",
